{"id": "Db-y7rjhceQ", "title": "Video by krishnachaytanyaa", "description": "Cron jobs are how a server runs your code on a schedule, without you being there.\nThe five stars in a crontab line are five fields: minute, hour, day of month, month, day of week. A star means “any value”. Cron wakes up every single minute and checks all five against the clock. All five match, your script runs. One says no, nothing happens.\nThat is why * * * * * runs 1,440 times a day and 0 3 * * * runs exactly once, at 3am. Same server, same line, one field changed.\nThis is the cron syntax behind Kubernetes CronJob and Jenkins. systemd timers solve the same problem with their own.\nWhich cron schedule have you actually had to debug in production? Drop it below.\nFollow @krishnachaytanyaa for system design and backend concepts explained visually.\n.\n.\n#systemdesign #softwarearchitecture #cronjob #crontab #linux", "timestamp": 1786626005, "channel": "krishnachaytanyaa", "uploader": "Krishna Chaitanya | Solutions Architect", "uploader_id": "27131031756", "like_count": 320, "comment_count": 4, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "duration": 9.006999969482422, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-3498442913650643a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 30.146, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr20-5.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQMphqD_Qy6Uv6ZcnZVKUAMM4FDsfVGknhrOWUTxLTuA0J2Fh59lIFVHJz8sZMehivwlcRzAPdLHfQANo7d716xYTv3DVg2-ecS1RVY.mp4?_nc_cat=107&_nc_oc=AdprxibFbigT2R7vjgF1F2o8P2MIKygPE1Dn8V7NOVcwd85DHdvj-qHErCg5IjAvERoefKYhrVRo8GkxlV8Yx0EN&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr20-5.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=hECO3ZLi018Q7kNvwHgqM02&%3D&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=ceUWSggVAb1JJPZsqcrNvw&_nc_ss=7a22e&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQG6j_tKLYXbb7IxX0dVWTkMfRGKcrXqs8mbTDK35Pq82A&oe=6A834B98", "manifest_stream_number": 0, "is_dash_periods": true, "protocol": "https", "audio_ext": "m4a", "video_ext": "none", "vbr": 0, "abr"